// Charge capacity is built, not found. A tower with no cell bank has
// nowhere to put a day's surplus and browns out the moment the sun
// goes down; a tower that has spent the floor space to bank enough
// rides the night out (SYSTEMS.md §1.2 exit criteria).
#![enable(implicit_some)]
RoomDef(
    id: "room.cell_bank",
    name: "Cell Bank",
    short: "BNK",
    // **Opens once the burner is lit**, which is where the opening
    // ends. `SYSTEMS.md` §6.11: a first-turn menu with twenty cards on
    // it is the loudest thing in the game and says nothing, so the menu
    // grows as the tower does. This is a fact about the tower, not the
    // player — the journal (§5.7) is the other kind of unlock and can
    // only filter a menu.
    // Visible after the Burner as the power branch's long-term answer.
    // Its cell + mechanism price keeps it aspirational without hiding
    // the reason those materials matter from the build menu.
    unlocked_by: "room.burner",
    category: Energy,
    // One slot. A rack of cells stacks upward rather than outward.
    width: 1,
    // **Cells, not poles, from M5.** This used to be 8 poles, which
    // made "I keep browning out at night" a problem you spent your way
    // out of. Costing cells means the answer runs through the
    // sun-forge, which is the largest charge sink in the tower — so
    // raising your charge ceiling costs charge. The first place in the
    // game where fixing a problem costs the resource the problem is
    // about (`SYSTEMS.md` §5.3).
    // Cells hold charge; a fitted switching mechanism makes them a
    // usable local reserve. This gives precision infrastructure a
    // durable mechanisms sink without making the emergency generator
    // depend on late metalwork.
    build_cost: [
        // One fabricated cell establishes the late storage branch;
        // additional cells remain a competing use for lantern masts.
        CostEntryDef(item: "item.charge_cells", amount: 1),
        CostEntryDef(item: "item.mechanisms", amount: 1),
    ],
    bank: BankDef(
        // A full night's worst case (striding, lights, one continuous
        // thornwright, no sun) costs on the order of 6,000 charge —
        // about four of these. Real floor space for real security.
        capacity: 1500,
        // **Half a burner's worth of pipe** (`SYSTEMS.md` §6.36). A
        // burner supplies 8 a tick; this supplies 4, so a bank helps a
        // tower spend harder without being a cheaper reactor than a
        // reactor. That ordering is deliberate — FTL's backup battery
        // is a stopgap for exactly the same reason, and if storage were
        // the efficient way to buy supply nobody would ever build the
        // second burner.
        //
        // It is also what makes "build another bank" a real answer to a
        // brown-out. Before the rail, capacity bought endurance only,
        // and a tower with a full bank that could not spend fast enough
        // had nothing to do about it.
        discharge_per_tick: 4,
    ),
)
